From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:22:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Rename 3GPP-IPv6-DNS-Server to
 3GPP-IPv6-DNS-Servers

3GPP TS 29.061 names sub-attribute 17 3GPP-IPv6-DNS-Servers throughout:
clause 16.4.7.2 ('17 - 3GPP-IPv6-DNS-Servers', a list of one or more
IPv6 addresses), the clause 16.4.7.1 table, table 9a (clause 16a.5) and
the AAA ABNF in clause 16a.4.2. Checked against V18.1.0.

Renaming an AVP renames its display filter field
(diameter.3GPP-IPv6-DNS-Server becomes diameter.3GPP-IPv6-DNS-Servers),
so saved filters and profiles using the old name need updating.
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
index 65e5a13..52ae868 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
   <avp name="3GPP-GGSN-IPv6-Address" code="16" mandatory="must" may-encrypt="yes" protected="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
     <type type-name="OctetString"/>
   </avp>
-  <avp name="3GPP-IPv6-DNS-Server" code="17" mandatory="must" may-encrypt="yes" protected="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
+  <avp name="3GPP-IPv6-DNS-Servers" code="17" mandatory="must" may-encrypt="yes" protected="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
     <type type-name="OctetString"/>
   </avp>
   <avp name="3GPP-SGSN-MCC-MNC" code="18" mandatory="must" may-encrypt="yes" protected="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="TGPP">
